## Async ownership and inference cancellation

GPUI `Task<()>` ownership prevents stale UI writes, but task drop alone is not
enough for queued or active inference. Search, chat, imports, and embedding
plans retain both the GPUI task and one parent
`u_forge_core::queue::CancellationToken`.

- Replacing an operation calls `supersede()` on the old token.
- User Stop/close calls `cancel()`.
- Every child queue/search/ingest call receives the same token.
- Completion remains observed after cancellation so runtime and GPU leases are
  known to be released; epoch/generation checks only reject late presentation.
- `Cancelled`, `Superseded`, timeout classes, provider failure, and worker loss
  remain distinct at the UI boundary.

Path-picker browse and other non-inference prompts still store their GPUI task
handle. Replacing a prompt drops the old task so a stale portal response cannot
overwrite newer modal state.

