## Modal overlay — centered blocking dialog

Use `deferred()` to float a modal above all sibling panels. The backdrop is a full-screen absolute div; `deferred()` ensures it paints after all siblings.

```rust
// In Render impl — append after the main content tree
deferred(
    div()
        .id("modal-backdrop")
        .absolute().top_0().left_0()
        .w_full().h_full()
        .occlude()
        .flex().items_center().justify_center()
        .bg(rgba(0x0000008c))
        .child(dialog_div),
)
```

The backdrop must call `.occlude()` so its hitbox blocks hover, clicks, and
scroll handling from reaching controls behind the modal.

Dialog structure: fixed-width `div` (~520 px) with a dark title bar row, a body row (inputs), and a footer row (Cancel + Confirm). Keep the entity stored as `Option<(Kind, Entity<Modal>)>` in `AppView`; drop (set to `None`) on cancel or confirm.

`PathPickerModal` (`src/path_picker.rs`) is the canonical example — reusable in-app file/folder picker that pre-populates a `TextFieldView` from a configured path and offers a "…" browse button that calls `cx.prompt_for_paths()`.

```rust
// Conditionally render the modal
.when(self.path_picker.is_some(), |root| {
    root.child(self.path_picker.as_ref().unwrap().1.clone())
})
```

**Why not the native picker alone:** `cx.prompt_for_paths(PathPromptOptions { … })` on Linux (ashpd XDG portal) has no initial-directory parameter. The custom modal pre-populates a path field from config and lets the user edit it directly, then optionally invoke the native picker to browse from scratch.

