## Conditional menu item grey-out (no disabled widget)

GPUI CE 0.3.3 has no built-in disabled state. Pattern: build the base element outside an `if/else`, then conditionally attach interactivity.

```rust
.child({
    let el = div()
        .id("import-data-item")
        .flex().items_center()
        .h(px(28.0)).px_3().text_sm();
    if has_schema {
        el.text_color(rgba(0xcdd6f4ff))
          .cursor_pointer()
          .hover(|s| s.bg(rgba(0x45475a88)))
          .on_mouse_down(MouseButton::Left, cx.listener(|this, _: &MouseDownEvent, window, cx| {
              this.file_menu_open = false;
              this.do_import_data_picker(window, cx);
          }))
    } else {
        el.text_color(rgba(0xcdd6f450))   // 50% alpha — visually dimmed
    }
    .child("Import Data…")
})
```

The disabled branch omits `.cursor_pointer()`, `.hover()`, and `.on_mouse_down()` — the item renders but accepts no clicks. Use `rgba(color, 0x50)` (50% alpha) for the dim text. Applied in `app_view/render.rs` for Import Data (greyed when `!schema_loaded`), Export Data (greyed when `node_count == 0`), Clear Schema (greyed when `!schema_loaded`), Clear Data (greyed when `node_count == 0`).

